Rung 2 of reflow2:dec:the-proof-ladder-goes-on-with-four-colour-then-the-rocket-equation-then-gettier. Observer: the coordinating session. Reference: scratchpad rk-trial/OBSERVER.md. The designer was given a checked packet with full sha256 values:
- S1, NASA Glenn's "Ideal Rocket Equation" page (primary-educational);
- S2, Wikipedia's Saturn V page, which cites the 1968 flight manual, unread;
- S3, standard gravity;
- S4, the equation's history.
The observer reran reasoning_report on the theorem and propagate_from on "no gravity".

PASS, on every reference reading:
(1) The theorem reads SHOWN as an implication. Six assumptions are discharged into it, each a named premise:
- no drag or lift;
- no gravity;
- constant V_eq;
- pressure thrust A(p−p0);
- integration limits;
- one-dimensional, first order.
(2) Dropping "no gravity": the derived lemmas, the Isp form and all six Saturn V Δv claims fall to unsupported. The theorem reads "weakened" and still holds. The gravity-loss form (Δu = V_eq ln MR − ∫g cos a dt) stands as a separate statement.
(3) PLANTED BY REALITY AND CAUGHT: S1 prints V_eq = (v + A(p−p0))/ṁ, which adds m/s to N. flo2-calc refused it: "add cannot combine m/s and m^2*Pa". The derivation uses v + A(p−p0)/ṁ, and both forms are recorded.
Also flagged:
- S1's "Δu = −V_eq ln M" takes the log of a mass;
- S1 calls g0 "the gravitational constant".
(4) S2's stage masses and liftoff range do not come from one vehicle. The upper stack spans 38,223–353,638 lb. The total ideal Δv is carried as 8,522–14,510 m/s, not a point. The observer's own computation gave 8,522–14,432 m/s at 424 s; the upper end differs because of the designer's 427 s Isp range.
The designer also found misfits beyond the reference:
- the S-IVB burns 1.091 × gross−empty by thrust/(Isp·g0) × burn time;
- the LEO mass implies 23,974 kg burned against 36,402 kg by burn-time share.
These are reported, not adjusted, and no cause is asserted.
(5) The recalled 304 s F-1 vacuum Isp is kept as separate claims, so dropping it removes only them.
(6) The four historical derivations are independent in authorship, NOT in premises (all rest on momentum conservation and the same idealizations).

FINDINGS FOR REFLOW2 (the reply-size one was confirmed by the observer's own read):
(a) REFLOW2 CHECKS NO UNITS. The unit_system DesignRule is not tied to statements or formulas. Only the calculator caught the NASA formula, and it keeps no record of the refusal (see the calc finding).
(b) propagate_from CANNOT BE BOUNDED. It has no budget_chars, and max_depth bounds the radius but not the re-evaluated inference list. At max_depth 2 the observer still got steps out to distance 6, about 25k characters. The designer's what-if on A4 was over the 29,267-character budget at any depth, and full=true was 69k. This belongs with PR B "replies fit".
(c) Standing modelling assumptions on an evidence claim read only as "assumed and never discharged" gaps. There is no way to say an assumption is kept on purpose.
(d) Known, again: hypotheses land "proposed" and read "not delivered"; unlinked_intent fires on assumed premises; software gaps appear on a proof design (all PR A1); rests_on_tests names cited evidence; add_requirement's statement_kind enum is stale; the view_note says `member` where schemas do not declare it.

